    "created_at": "2018-03-08T12:25:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-08T12:25:06Z",
    "body": "I think the abort event is important and needed because it reflects direct action and intent initiated by users.  Users canceling/aborting/stopping page load is also a valid stage in an application's lifecycle.  Making this event visible allows for more robust application development and gives options to developers when needed.\r\n\r\nThe browsers already correctly execute the stop/cancel functionality internally.  Browsers would only need to report when that functionality occurs by firing `abort`.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
